.page profile 5 the login shell's start-up file

# DESCRIPTION
`/Hakurei/etc/profile` is read by gapsh(1) when it starts as a login shell, which is how init(8) starts it. It is an ordinary gapsh script. The shipped file:

    export PATH=/bin:/sbin:/usr/bin
    export TERM=xterm
    export EDITOR=pnote
    export PAGER=patchouli-pager

    alias ll='ls -l'
    alias la='ls -la'
    alias l='ls -CF'
    alias ..='cd ..'
    alias grep='grep --color=auto'
    alias cls='clear'
    alias shutdown='poweroff'
    alias exorcise='kill -9'
    alias spellcards='ps'
    alias netherworld='ls /Netherworld'

`EDITOR` and `PAGER` are what programs that need to show or edit text look at: the manual viewer uses `PAGER`. A user's own `~/.gaprc` is read afterwards by interactive shells and can override all of it.

# FILES
@ /Hakurei/etc/profile
    This file.
@ ~/.gaprc
    Personal additions.

# SEE ALSO
gapsh(1), motd(5), alias(1), export(1)
